cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "fhir-scorecard: grades for publicly observable FHIR endpoints"
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Kelly-Reif
    given-names: Chelsea
repository-code: "https://github.com/ChelseaKR/fhir-scorecard"
url: "https://chelseakr.github.io/fhir-scorecard/"
abstract: >-
  Deterministic grades for the public discovery surfaces of FHIR endpoints across health payers,
  providers, EHR vendors, and reference servers. Derived only from unauthenticated
  CapabilityStatement and SMART discovery documents, with spec-cited findings, capability drift
  tracking, and daily availability observations. Observational; not an audit, a ranking of care
  quality, or a statement about regulatory compliance.
keywords:
  - FHIR
  - health information exchange
  - interoperability
  - CMS interoperability rule
  - Patient Access API
  - open data
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-08-16"
